  "[action] (to Wang Lung) O-lan responds hesitantly.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"If I were a great merchant and you a great lady, I would never have said such a thing to you, never. For you are as lovely as a field of flowers, and I am only a poor farmer.\"",
  "[silence] (to Wang Lung) O-lan says nothing.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"But you are only a woman, and I have said a foolish thing. Now tell me this, have you ever seen any woman in the great house, any woman whom you have seen with your own eyes?\"",
